htforward and performant. Nice work on this user-facing improvement. PR-2106 (fraud-engine): Ethan Williams tuned velocity rules for card-not-present transactions, balancing bypass risk with proprietary thresholds. The careful review of rule changes and threshold confidentiality is appreciated. PR-2107 (billing-core): Fatima Hassan localized invoice currency formatting, improving international usability. The use of Intl.NumberFormat is a clean and effective solution. Well done on this polish. PR-2108 (payments-api): Grace Lindgren refactored refund handler error mapping, quarantining flaky tests and improving error code clarity. The monitoring setup ensures ongoing stability. Thanks for addressing this tricky area. PR-2109 (checkout-gateway): Hiro Tanaka implemented exponential backoff for upstream processor retries, significantly enhancing reliability under load. The retry logic is robust and well-integrated. Excellent contribution. PR-2110 (payments-api): Imani Brooks added webhook signature validation with constant-time comparison, strengthening security against forgery. The implementation is precise and well-reviewed. Great security enhancement. PR-2111 (payouts-worker): Jamal Foster moved the payout cron to a queue-based scheduler, addressing a double-fire issue with a dedupe guard. The rollback and incident postmortem show thorough incident handling. PR-2112 (billing-core): Kalea Wong added a tiered fee calculation engine with customer-specific pricing rules under contract. The solution is flexible and respects confidentiality. Nice work on this complex billing logic. PR-2113 (ledger-service): Liam O'Sullivan reconciled late-arriving settlement files with path traversal protections. The repeated CI timeouts were tracked to infra issues, showing good investigative follow-up. PR-2114 (api-gateway): Maya Goldberg deprecated the v1 charges endpoint with appropriate sunset headers, aligning with approved timelines. The clear communication in headers supports smooth