l usability. The use of Intl.NumberFormat is a clean and effective solution. Well done on this polish.\n\nPR-2108 (payments-api): Grace Lindgren refactored refund handler error mapping, quarantining flaky tests and improving error code clarity. The monitoring setup ensures ongoing stability. Thanks for addressing this tricky area.\n\nPR-2109 (checkout-gateway): Hiro Tanaka implemented exponential backoff for upstream processor retries, significantly enhancing reliability under load. The retry logic is robust and well-integrated. Excellent contribution.\n\nPR-2110 (payments-api): Imani Brooks added webhook signature validation with constant-time comparison, strengthening security against forgery. The implementation is precise and well-reviewed. Great security enhancement.\n\nPR-2111 (payouts-worker): Jamal Foster moved the payout cron to a queue-based scheduler, addressing a double-fire issue with a dedupe guard. The rollback and incident postmortem show thorough incident handling.\n\nPR-2112 (billing-core): Kalea Wong added a tiered fee calculation engine with customer-specific pricing rules under contract. The solution is flexible and respects confidentiality. Nice work on this complex billing logic.\n\nPR-2113 (ledger-service): Liam O'Sullivan reconciled late-arriving settlement files with path traversal protections. The repeated CI timeouts were tracked to infra issues, showing good investigative follow-up.\n\nPR-2114 (api-gateway): Maya Goldberg deprecated the v1 charges endpoint with appropriate sunset headers, aligning with approved timelines. The clear communication in headers supports smooth client migration.\n\nPR-2115 (payments-api): Noah Bennett's purge stale card fingerprints job is currently disabled due to legal hold, with build issues resolved. The caution here is well-placed given pending litigation.\n\nPR-2116 (merchant-dashboard): Olivia Nguyen improved accessible keyboard navigation for dispute forms, including MIME validation for evidence uploads. This enhances usability and compliance.\n\nPR-2117 (fraud-engine): Priya Sharma added structured logging to the scoring pipeline, ensuring no sensitive PAN or CVV data is emitted. This improves observability while maintaining privacy.\n\nPR-2118 (checkout-gateway): Aiden Mercer cached processor BIN lookups, reducing latency and load. The TTL-based cache is a smart optimization.\n\nPR-2119 (auth-service): Ava Patel added MFA step-up for high-value payouts with fallback protections, rolling out cautiously to a beta cohort. This strengthens security for sensitive transactions.\n\nPR-2120 (ledger-service): Brianna Okafor backfilled currency columns for legacy entries, with DBA review scheduled after migration dry-run failures. This cleanup supports accurate reporting.\n\nPR-2121 (merchant-dashboard): Daniela Cruz added CSV export for settlement reports, enabling easier data analysis. The implementation is user-friendly and efficient.\n\nPR-2122 (payments-api): Fatima Hassan rate-limited the card tokenization endpoint to prevent abuse, with limits reviewed against card-testing patterns. This is a valuable protective measure.\n\nPR-2123 (payouts-worker): Grace Lindgren implemented graceful shutdown for payout consumers, ensuring clean exits on SIGTERM. This improves system stability.\n\nPR-2124 (api-gateway): Imani Brooks added request ID propagation, fixing lint issues and addressing header rename impacts. This aids in tracing and debugging.\n\nPR-2125 (billing-core): Jamal Foster added proration for mid-cycle plan changes, calculating credits and charges accurately. This enhances billing fairness.\n\nPR-2126 (fraud-engine): Liam O'Sullivan replaced regex email checks with a parser to avoid ReDoS risks. This improves input validation robustness.\n\nPR-2127 (api-gateway): Maya Goldberg added OpenAPI schema for v2 disputes, revealing fields for an upcoming product launch. This prepares the API for new features.\n\nPR-2128 (merchant-dashboard): Olivia Nguyen refactored state management for the onboarding wizard, addressing snapshot test breakages and including KYC steps. This stabilizes onboarding flows.\n\nPR-2129 (ledger-service): Priya Sharma added read replica routing for reports, optimizing query performance. This is a solid infrastructure improvement.\n\nPR-2130 (checkout-gateway): Hiro Tanaka added a circuit breaker for the 3DS provider, preventing silent authentication skips. This enhances payment security.\n\nPR-2131 (payouts-worker): Carlos Reyes-Vega implemented currency conversion at payout time with treasury markup, aligning with internal policy. This ensures accurate financial handling.\n\nPR-2132 (fraud-engine): Ethan Williams added device fingerprint feature extraction, respecting vendor contract constraints. This enriches fraud detection inputs.\n\nPR-2133 (billing-core): Kalea Wong added a dunning retry schedule for failed invoices, avoiding duplicate charges on network timeouts. This improves collections reliability.\n\nPR-2134 (payments-api): Noah Bennett cleaned up deprecated charge status enums, resolving deploy issues and routine maintenance. This keeps the codebase tidy.\n\nPR-2135 (merchant-dashboard): Daniela Cruz added dark mode for the dashboard shell, enhancing user experience with theme support. Nice visual upgrade.\n\nPR-2136 (api-gateway): Grace Lindgren scoped API keys to merchant sub-accounts, verified by sub-account isolation tests. This is a key security enhancement.", 'reply_to': None} status=200 email_id=message-bd1358a4f2 recipients=['elena.park@brightline-sys.com'] attachments=[]
